'''
## 📌 Plot Part — Theory Summary

### 1. Predicted Values

```python
y_pred = model.predict(X)
```

Trained Linear Regression model se predicted values obtain karte hain.

* `y` → Actual values
* `y_pred` → Predicted values

---

### 2. Scatter Plot

```python
plt.scatter(y_pred, y)
```

Actual aur predicted values ke relationship ko **dots/points** ke form mein show karta hai.

* **X-axis** → Predicted Values
* **Y-axis** → Actual Values

---

### 3. Regression Line

```python
m, b = np.polyfit(y_pred, y, 1)
```

`np.polyfit()` data points ke liye **best-fit straight line** ke slope (`m`) aur intercept (`b`) calculate karta hai.

```python
x_line = np.array([y_pred.min(), y_pred.max()])
y_line = m * x_line + b
```

Ye regression line ke X aur Y coordinates generate karta hai.

---

### 4. Line Plot

```python
plt.plot(x_line, y_line, color='red')
```

Calculated regression line ko graph par draw karta hai.

`color='red'` se line **red** दिखाई देती है.

---

### 5. Labels & Title

```python
plt.xlabel("Predicted Values")
plt.ylabel("Actual Values")
plt.title("Actual vs Predicted with Regression Line")
```

Graph ke X-axis, Y-axis aur title ko define karta hai.

---

### 6. Display Plot

```python
plt.show()
```

Complete graph ko display karta hai.

### 🔑 Overall

```text
Predicted Values + Actual Values
              ↓
        Scatter Plot
              ↓
       Best-Fit Regression Line
              ↓
      Actual vs Predicted Graph
```

'''
